{
  "candidates": [
    {
      "id": "opening-reads-in-collect",
      "summary": "collect gains an opening phase after the shard loop that reads the interval's first block, each epoch boundary's slot and header, and each implementation's runtime code into a journaled, checkpointed epoch-evidence class; build discovers the epochs from that journal, ships the code as a component the epoch table names, and check re-hashes it."
    },
    {
      "id": "epochs-subcommand",
      "summary": "A third network command, epochs, runs after collect and before reconcile: it scans the staged logs for upgrades and reads the first block, the boundary slots and headers and the runtime code into its own journal; collect is unchanged and build and check consume the journal the same way."
    },
    {
      "id": "operator-supplied-evidence",
      "summary": "The shipped shape: the operator reads the first block, the slots and the runtime code out of band and hands build an epoch table plus a code file; the release preserves the code bytes but no journal binds them to a request the collector made."
    },
    {
      "id": "trace-mandatory",
      "summary": "Keep the three evidence classes fixed and add the opening reads to collect; the live run then needs a primary that serves trace_filter, which no provider reachable from this session without a credential does."
    }
  ],
